# Return opens the row the cursor is on, and the cursor stops at the end.
#
# Eight Downs on a six-row list: the sixth lands on the last row and the rest
# have nowhere to go. Clamping, not wrapping — a list whose end you can see
# should not teleport you back to the top. Return then opens THAT row, which
# is asserted through text only its transcript has, so the assertion fails if
# the cursor was on any other row. That line used to be "the diff touches a
# generated file", from a reply hanabi had written for itself; the thread is
# Puffin's `mock-outcome-2` ported verbatim now (feat/vis-fixture), so the
# assertion moved to a sentence of the ported reply. It is deliberately short
# enough to sit inside one rendered line: the transcript emits one label per
# WRAPPED line, so a phrase that straddles a wrap can never match.
#
# The view is switched by coordinate because every smart view shares one
# debug name (see smart_view_switch.e2e, same click).
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}

click 60 151
wait_frames 6
expect_text "Blocked on you"

key DOWN
wait_frames 6
key DOWN
wait_frames 6
key DOWN
wait_frames 6
key DOWN
wait_frames 6
key DOWN
wait_frames 6
key DOWN
wait_frames 6
key DOWN
wait_frames 6
key DOWN
wait_frames 6
key ENTER
wait_frames 60
expect_text "That is the Autograph key"
